No, you're doing exactly right.

An (unguaranteed!) wish at the beginning might help you a bit farther.

But a light source in the mines prevents you from examining too many
floor tiles, thus not unnecessarily increasing the number of traps you
would step onto without light. Worst are polymorph or magic traps, IMO.
These can be quasi-instant-death reasons, at least ruin your game.

If I have no light source I completely avoid the mines. If I explored
much of the dungeon until the castle and found no light source, I enter
the mines, dig down until I reach minetown to obtain some lighting in
that guaranteed store.

As others also pointed out, it increases speed in exploring the mazes.
The trap problem described above also applies.

There are lot of possibilities to get wishes, even guaranteed ones.
But permanent light is rare.

